    "created_at": "2025-05-21T14:32:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-21T14:32:27Z",
    "body": "Separate from preloads, the link header is also used for compression dictionaries to trigger the async fetch of a dictionary that would be used for future requests. For example, an API call with a JSON response might link to the compression dictionary for the API and future API calls would use it.\n\nPresumably the dictionary could be loaded by script injecting a link tag instead but, at least for this case, the subresource does have all of the context it needs to specify the dictionary.",
